   "text": {
    "L1": "Plants are useful in many parts of our lives, not just on our plates.",
    "L2": "Some people think we use plants only for food. That idea is not true.",
    "L3": "We use plants for food, medicine, shelter, and craft.",
    "L4": "Different plant parts can be food: carrot is a root, potato is a stem, spinach is a leaf, and cauliflower is a flower.",
    "L5": "In aloo-gobi, roti and dal, we use a stem, flowers and seeds.",
    "L6": "Plants also give us medicines, houses and useful craft materials such as bamboo, jute and cotton.",
    "L7": "A banana-leaf plate rots naturally, unlike plastic, which can pollute for a long time.",
    "L8": "Never taste an unknown leaf or berry. Always ask an adult first."
   },
